<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Barton returns six weeks after starting sertraline 50 mg. She has had four sessions of cognitive behavioral therapy and has kept a daily plan of small tasks and walks. She went back to work three weeks ago on a 25-hour week and has kept to it. Her mood is a little better on most days and she can concentrate on one report at a time, but she still feels flat, tires by mid-afternoon, and sleeps about five and a half hours. She has had no side effects since the first week and has missed no doses. She has had no suicidal thoughts. She has seen two friends each week. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>Somewhat better mood and concentration; still flat and tired</td></tr><tr><td>Psychotherapy</td><td>Four CBT sessions; daily activity plan</td></tr><tr><td>Work</td><td>Back three weeks on a 25-hour week</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About five and a half hours</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts</td></tr><tr><td>PHQ-9</td><td>12, down from 18</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

