    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder, recurrent, with partial response at six weeks (F33.1)</content>. PHQ-9 12, down 33 percent from 18: a partial response, short of the 50 percent that defines response, on a well-tolerated dose. Suicide risk remains low. [S]<list><item>Increase sertraline to 100 mg each morning.</item><item>Nurse telephone check in two weeks for side effects and safety.</item><item>Continue weekly CBT.</item><item>Collaborative safety plan reviewed and unchanged; 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline and the clinic number confirmed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Occupational burnout (Z73.0)</content>. Managing the 25-hour week. [S]<list><item>Increase to 35 hours a week now and to no more than 45 hours in a month if her mood keeps improving; still no field deployment.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9</td><td>Baseline, then at least monthly during acute treatment; every 2 to 4 weeks in continuation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>12, down 33 percent from 18: partial response; dose increased</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide risk reassessment (C-SSRS Since Last Visit and PHQ-9 item 9)</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No suicidal thoughts, intent, plan, or behavior since the last visit; PHQ-9 item 9 scored 0. Protective factors unchanged; safety plan reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Adherence and adverse-effect review</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No missed doses; no side effects since the first week</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Tolerability check two weeks after the dose increase</td><td>2 weeks after each dose change</td><td>Due</td><td>Nurse telephone check booked for two weeks from today</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Psychotherapy, activity, sleep, work hours, and social contact</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Four CBT sessions; 25-hour week; sleep about five and a half hours; friends twice a week</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Lithium, anticonvulsant, or antipsychotic monitoring (levels, metabolic tests, AIMS)</td><td>Only on those drugs</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Treated with an SSRI only</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Response (PHQ-9 down by at least 50 percent) by twelve weeks. In progress; target 2026-04-14 [S]</item><item>Remission (PHQ-9 below 5) and continuation treatment for at least twelve months after remission. In progress; target 2026-06-16 [S]</item><item>Sleep at least six hours most nights. In progress; target 2026-04-14 [S]</item><item>Phased return to work at no more than 45 hours a week, with no field deployment for at least six months. In progress; target 2026-06-16 [S]</item><item>Time with friends or her faith community at least twice a week. In progress; target 2026-06-16 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Nurse telephone check in two weeks; depression review in six weeks. Next scheduled visit 2026-04-14: twelve-week depression treatment review. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
